            <ArticleTitle>Case report: single coronary artery with ischemia and sudden cardiac arrest.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>121-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Single coronary artery (SCA) is a very rare finding. Although most cases of SCA are found incidentally on coronary angiography, it can potentially lead to different clinical repercussions.1, 2 Herein we describe a patient with SCA who had unstable angina with subsequent sudden cardiac arrest, and we provide a brief review of the recent literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
